From c1e3d7fc7746baf66a1b91c2e1a87576b95e4dfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:28:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Batch: copies of the states of the materials by kernels of
 MFEM

`batch::MFEMFieldOperations` implements the field operations of MGIS
(copies and fills of views with any strides, as used by the update and
the revert of a material data manager) with kernels of MFEM
(`mfem::forall_switch`), on the device of MFEM or on the host. It is the
first source of the library compiled as CUDA code when MFEM is compiled
with CUDA (`src/Batch`, `include/MFEMMGIS/Batch`).

`Material::updateMaterialStates` and `Material::revertMaterialStates`
synchronize the arrays on the host and update or revert the states with
these operations, on the host where MGIS uses the arrays. They are used
by the behaviour integrators and by the point-wise models, whose update
and revert did not synchronize the arrays before.

MFEMFieldOperationsTest: copies between the point by point and the
component by component layouts, copy of a uniform value, fill of one
component, on the host and on the device, with the cpu, debug and cuda
devices.
